# Run outputs split cleanly by size, and the split IS the payload/finding boundary: on the first
# 27B capture, 5.2 GB of `.npz` residual streams against ~57 KB of `.json` reports. The findings
# go to the remote so the repo alone shows what was measured; the payloads never do, because a
# capture is reproducible from the recorded seed, revision and config, and a 5 GB blob in git
# history is permanent. `battery.json` is the exception on both counts — 4 MB, and it is the
# rendered stimulus set (regenerable, golden-parity tested), not a result.
runs/**
!runs/**/
!runs/**/*.json
runs/**/battery.json
# Smoke runs are FAKE-BACKEND output. They are the right thing to keep locally and the wrong
# thing to publish: a report named like a finding, holding numbers no model produced.
runs/*smoke*/**
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Fitted artifacts are large and run-specific; the drop-in slot keeps only its README.
results/artifacts/*
!results/artifacts/README.md

# Fetched norm VALUES are third-party (Warriner supplement; NRC-VAD is research-use-only and
# non-redistributable). The provenance manifest is ours and stays; the values do not.
data/norms/*
!data/norms/MANIFEST.json
